-- 075-ties: rank under ties must be value-only. Twin of 075-ties.bqn. (was t2-ties)
-- The tie law: equal gold, equal rank. On 5 5 3 the answer is 1 1 0, dense; the ordinal 1 2 0 is the refuted form.
-- rank(Gold) on the tied fixture 5 5 3 must produce the dense rank 1 1 0 (the tied 5s share their rank); the stable ordinal ⍋⍋ answer 1 2 0 is the unlawful form this witness exists to refute.
-- The Ord anchors, the swap(0,1) counterexample, and the exhaustive Sym(3) quantification of the dense law are BQN-internal witnesses, left to the .bqn twin. rank is zero-initialized scaffold (the .bqn mints it fresh).
--! registry ../registries/075-ties.reg
--! expect rank = 1 1 0

Unit , Rank = rank(Gold)
